From 0107b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] bsd: declare delay() for polaris_gpu_pwron via kern/clock.h

DELAY() in bsd/arm/param.h expands to delay(), which is declared in
osfmk/kern/clock.h under XNU_KERNEL_PRIVATE.  bsd/dev/polaris_rpmh.c
already includes that header in the same position for the same reason.
Without it the arm64 kernel build stops with "call to undeclared
function 'delay'".

diff --git a/bsd/dev/polaris_gpu_pwron.c b/bsd/dev/polaris_gpu_pwron.c
index e7f71c8..4fc9c36 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/polaris_gpu_pwron.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/polaris_gpu_pwron.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include <sys/systm.h>
 #include <pexpert/pexpert.h>
 #include <vm/pmap.h>
+#include <kern/clock.h>
 #include <machine/machine_routines.h>
 #include <dev/polaris_gpu_pwr.h>
 
